        "endingText": "The white house was empty. Why would there be anyone there? There was no point anymore. America was no longer the same. It never would be. Mitt stood alone. The emptiness. The quiet. It was driving him insane. This was supposed to be the moment for him to prove himself. He walked across empty halls. He looked at the portraits hung on the walls. The forgotten presidents. This was his fate. He won it all but would just be forgotten. They would focus on what led to it. Not on him. He walked to the oval office. Not even the vice president was there. He took a deep breath and started writing his note. He wrote for hours, moving to more and more pages. To anyone who would've been there it might look like he's hard at work. The truth was that he was writing a note for every scenario. He thought about al the ways this could end. His mind was empty now, filled with the cheers he had hoped to hear. He knew that things would never be the same. No one cared anymore. No one was surprised that he won. He wasn't chosen because he was wanted but because there was no other choice. Ayers wasn't a candidate. He was a lamb. Mitt felt his hands tightening and tightening as he wrote. The page ripping as the pen broke. Ink smeared the papers. His notes ruined. Mitt looked at it, unfazed. His face was completely blank, nearly robotic. He stood up, pulled the chair to the table and walked out. Out of the office. Out of the White house. Out of America's mind.",
